WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.990
Before weather satellites, a hurricane could arrive with almost no warning.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:16.280
The first weather satellite sent its first cloud pictures in 1960.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.740
Today, satellites in geostationary orbit hover over the same spot

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.710
and watch storms grow minute by minute.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:36.730
At 35,786 kilometres, a satellite circles once a day, exactly as Earth turns.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.780
The price: a long, costly climb, and more radiation than in low orbit.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:52.930
A modern GOES satellite images half the planet every ten minutes, and a single storm every thirty seconds.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:58.550
Now look at your design. Every image is a warning that arrives in time.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:05.150
<v Roberto>Thirty-six thousand kilometres away, and it still saves lives every season.

